# snap6: OS software-timer service (globals g = 0x08817218: +0 armed list sorted by expiry, +4 expired
# stack, +0x14 cond waking timer thread T3). In the T0 overlay g+0 still points at 500 ms timer
# 0x0b3c77e8, which had ALREADY fired (+0x24 'expi', in-list +0x28 = 0, next 0; its 'time' node is
# queued to run-loop queue 0x0b439dec for T5 to complete). The overlay blocks were copied ~97 ms apart.
# T3 then re-fires it as the head forever and deadlocks in cancel-wait 0x080247c8 (Session 15).
# The real armed chain is intact: 0x0b3bd724 -> 0x0b3c07f8 -> 0x0b3bd764 (all 'run ', in-list 1).
0x08817218 0x0b3bd724
# snap6: button thread T25 (entry 0x08567808) is blocked (state 0x40, event 0x74) on its counting
# semaphore {count, event id} at 0x0899c0fc (handle stored at 0x08a7a700 on T25's stack), but the
# snapshot has count 0 instead of -1. The GPIO ISR's post (0x080019d0 via 0x08005e5c) signals the
# kernel event only when the old count is -1, so a Home press bumped it to 1 and never woke T25.
0x0899c0fc 0xffffffff
